  "hints": [
    "Copy `board` deeply first (`[list(row) for row in board]`) so the input board stays unmodified.",
    "Precompute row, col, and 3x3 box bitmasks/sets and always pick the empty cell with the FEWEST valid candidate digits next (MRV heuristic), solving even hard puzzles in a few milliseconds!",
    "Pseudocode:\n  find empty cell (r, c) with minimum candidates\n  try each digit d valid in row[r], col[c], box[r//3][c//3]\n  recurse; undo on backtrack"
  ],
